  "strategic_conclusions": [
    "Every serious competitor is deep in one lane (diff, fuzz, lint, contracts, virtualization, load, one protocol). None spans contract governance -> testing -> runtime drift -> replay safety -> performance gates -> deploy decisions on one shared model.",
    "The unified normalized-contract-graph plus shared result/artifact model is API Verity Lab's defensible differentiator; specialist depth (e.g., Schemathesis fuzzing maturity, Buf wire semantics) should be matched where feasible, not cloned wholesale.",
    "Drift detection and safety-gated replay with redaction are effectively uncontested niches among the compared tools.",
    "Consumer-impact + can-i-deploy currently requires adopting Pact's broker worldview; offering it over plain OpenAPI/GraphQL/gRPC contracts lowers adoption cost.",
    "Commercial boundary recommendation: keep Apache-2.0 core fully capable locally; reserve team/enterprise value for the self-hosted server (collaboration, policy, audit, workers) which competitors gate behind hosted products.",
    "Do NOT copy: hosted-only collaboration lock-in, AGPL constraints (k6), JVM-centrism (WireMock/Karate), or archived-tool assumptions (Dredd/Optic)."
  ]
